{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' papers/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Downloaded Papers\n\nThis directory contains the PDF corpus gathered for the Jacobson commutativity\nproject on fixed exponent `x^{p^3}=x` in characteristic `p`.\n\nChunked versions of the highest-priority papers are in `papers/pages/`.\n\n1. [Equational proofs of Jacobson's theorem](2310.05301_brandenburg_equational_proofs_jacobson.pdf)\n   - Author: Martin Brandenburg\n   - Year: 2023\n   - Source: arXiv:2310.05301, https://arxiv.org/pdf/2310.05301\n   - Why relevant: Central paper. Gives the equational framework, prime-power reductions, full proofs for `k=1` and `k=2`, and constructive Wedderburn reductions for general `k`. Contains explicit `8`- and `27`-ring examples and the main gap for `k=3`.\n\n2. [Elementary Proofs of Ring Commutativity Theorems](2601.12599_kinyon_machale_elementary_proofs_ring_commutativity.pdf)\n   - Authors: Michael K. Kinyon and Des MacHale\n   - Year: 2026\n   - Source: arXiv:2601.12599, https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.12599\n   - Why relevant: Develops elementary commutativity proofs for fixed exponents and records automated-theorem-prover support. The odd-exponent central-power lemma is directly relevant when `p` is odd.\n\n3. [Equational proofs for a theorem by Jacobson for a significant density of even exponents](daas_equational_proofs_density_even_exponents.pdf)\n   - Author: M. A. Daas\n   - Year: undated student note\n   - Source: https://pub.math.leidenuniv.nl/~daasma/Eqpfs.pdf redirected to a Google Drive copy\n   - Why relevant: Focuses on equational proofs for even exponents; useful context for `p=2`, where `p^3=8`.\n\n4. [Term Rewrite Rules for Finite Fields](burris_lawrence_1991_term_rewrite_rules_finite_fields.pdf)\n   - Authors: Stanley N. Burris and John Lawrence\n   - Year: 1991\n   - Source: https://www.math.uwaterloo.ca/~snburris/htdocs/MYWORKS/PAPERS/fields3.pdf\n   - Why relevant: Connects finite-field identities, equational theories, and term-rewrite systems for rings satisfying identities of the form `x^m=x`.\n\n5. [Commutativity Theorems: Examples in Search of Algorithms](wavrik_1999_commutativity_theorems_algorithms.pdf)\n   - Author: John Wavrik\n   - Year: 1999\n   - Source: https://mathweb.ucsd.edu/~jwavrik/pub/21_issac99.pdf\n   - Why relevant: Describes algorithmic approaches to noncommutative polynomial reductions for commutativity theorems.\n\n6. [A proof of Jacobson's theorem](dolan_1976_proof_of_jacobsons_theorem.pdf)\n   - Author: J. M. Dolan\n   - Year: 1976\n   - Source: Cambridge Core PDF\n   - Why relevant: Gives a short choice-free proof of Jacobson's theorem and clarifies the constructive lineage behind later equational work.\n\n7. [On the commutativity of J-rings](luh_1967_commutativity_of_j_rings.pdf)\n   - Author: Jiang Luh\n   - Year: 1967\n   - Source: Cambridge Core PDF\n   - Why relevant: Classical structural paper for fixed-exponent `J`-rings, including `p^k`-rings and finite-field decompositions.\n\n8. [Wedderburn's Theorem and a Theorem of Jacobson](herstein_1961_wedderburn_and_jacobson.pdf)\n   - Author: I. N. Herstein\n   - Year: 1961\n   - Source: https://www.carolynrabbott.com/uploads/3/0/8/1/30819067/herstein-wedderburn.pdf\n   - Why relevant: Historical source for elementary Wedderburn/Jacobson arguments.\n\n9. [Variations on a theme: Rings satisfying `x^3=x` are commutative](buckley_machale_2013_variations_x3_equals_x.pdf)\n   - Authors: Stephen M. Buckley and Des MacHale\n   - Year: 2013\n   - Source: https://archive.maths.nuim.ie/staff/sbuckley/Papers/bm_variations.pdf\n   - Why relevant: Low-exponent model of elementary commutativity proofs and centrality arguments.\n\n10. [A note on a theorem of Jacobson related to periodic rings](anderson_danchev_2020_periodic_rings_jacobson.pdf)\n    - Authors: D. D. Anderson and Peter Danchev\n    - Year: 2020\n    - Source: AMS Proceedings PDF\n    - Why relevant: Broader periodic-ring generalization of Jacobson-type commutativity.\n\n## Chunked PDFs\n\n- `papers/pages/2310.05301_brandenburg_equational_proofs_jacobson_manifest.txt`\n- `papers/pages/2601.12599_kinyon_machale_elementary_proofs_ring_commutativity_manifest.txt`\n- `papers/pages/daas_equational_proofs_density_even_exponents_manifest.txt`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"source .venv/bin/activate && python - <<'PY'\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader\nfrom pathlib import Path\npdf=Path('papers/2601.12599_kinyon_machale_elementary_proofs_ring_commutativity.pdf')\nreader=PdfReader(str(pdf))\nfor i,p in enumerate(reader.pages, start=1):\n    text=p.extract_text() or ''\n    if 'central' in text.lower() or '2m+1' in text or 'potent' in text.lower():\n        print(i, (text[:280].replace('\\\\n',' ')+'...'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
