{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"The literature review narrows the real gap: Brandenburg’s period criterion already covers `p=2`, `p=3`, and `p ≡ 2 mod 3`; only `p ≡ 1 mod 3` needs a new argument. I’m extracting the constructive Wedderburn section now because the `k=3` problem reduces there to two monomial identities."}}
